From fd57daf24412df20c6eeb89ef802ecd73436b069 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Opus 5.5" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 03:36:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] x11: list the monitors again when xrandr --setmonitor
 changes them

The monitor list is cached and dropped on a RandR screen change event.
Adding or removing a RandR 1.5 monitor (`xrandr --setmonitor`,
`--delmonitor`) sends none: the server tells clients with a
ConfigureNotify on the root window only, which the window manager
follows and winit did not, so a screen split while the application
ran was still one monitor to it until something else changed.

The event loop now also selects StructureNotify on the root window,
added to whatever this client already selected there, and a
ConfigureNotify for the root is handled as a RandR change: the list
is dropped and compared with the new one for scale factor changes.
The root's ConfigureNotify comes otherwise only with a change of the
screen's size, which already brings a RandR event, and the second
look at the list then finds nothing changed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/changelog/unreleased.md b/src/changelog/unreleased.md
index f5e747b..c35b2ec 100644
--- a/src/changelog/unreleased.md
+++ b/src/changelog/unreleased.md
@@ -51,3 +51,4 @@ changelog entry.
 - On Wayland, fix `Window::set_cursor` copying a custom cursor into a new buffer when it is already the window's cursor, and panicking when the buffer could not be allocated.
 - On X11, `Window::is_minimized` and `Window::is_maximized` no longer make a round trip to the X server on every call; `_NET_WM_STATE` is kept until a `PropertyNotify` says it changed.
 - On X11, list the RandR 1.5 monitors (those of `xrandr --listmonitors`, which the window manager goes by) where the server has them, rather than one per CRTC, so that `Fullscreen::Borderless` reaches each monitor of a screen split with `xrandr --setmonitor`.
+- On X11, list the monitors again when `xrandr --setmonitor` or `--delmonitor` changes them, which the server says with a `ConfigureNotify` on the root window and no RandR event.
